<title>CANADA: Arakis, partners sign Sudan oil deal.</title>
<headline>Arakis, partners sign Sudan oil deal.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Arakis Energy Corp and its three partners in a US$1 billion oil development project in Sudan have signed final agreements for the deal, Arakis chief executive John McLeod confirmed on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We signed it on Saturday,&quot; McLeod said in a phone interview.</p>
<p>Under the 25-year agreement, which was anxiously awaited by investors, Arakis has 25 percent, China National Petroleum Corp 40 percent, Malaysia state oil company Petronas 30 percent and the Sudan government five percent of the project to develop three blocks in Sudan's Muglad Basin.</p>
</text>
